# Metrics

> Back to [README](../README.md)

Every metric `@@EXPORTER_NAME@@` can emit, grouped by collector. This file is kept
truthful by `make docs-check` (part of `make check`, see
[CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md)'s Definition of Done): any metric or label
listed below that the code cannot actually produce fails the build. A metric the
code emits but this file doesn't document is only a warning: see
`internal/collector/docs_check_test.go`.

<!--
docs-check parses this file as a sequence of markdown tables, one metric per
row, in this exact 4-cell shape:

| `metric_name` | Type | `label1`, `label2` | Description |

- Metric name: backtick-quoted, matching the fqName passed to
  prometheus.NewDesc / HistogramOpts.Name in internal/collector/*.go.
- Type: Gauge, Counter, Histogram, or Summary (informational only, not
  itself verified by docs-check).
- Labels: each backtick-quoted, comma-separated; a literal `-` when the
  metric has none.
- Description: free text. Avoid a literal `|` character in this cell (it
  breaks table parsing).

Do not add a separate row for a Histogram's implicit `_bucket`/`_count`/`_sum`
series: they are derived from the parent row, not separate metrics as far
as docs-check (or PromQL) is concerned.

Standard Go runtime, process, and build-info metrics (from
`prometheus/client_golang/prometheus/collectors`, registered in
`cmd/@@EXPORTER_NAME@@/main.go`, disable the first two with
`--web.disable-exporter-metrics`) are intentionally not listed here: they are
not defined by this package, and are already documented by client_golang
itself. The same applies to `@@EXPORTER_NAME@@_build_info`, which comes from
client_golang's versioncollector and carries this exporter's own release
(version, revision, branch, goversion), and to
`promhttp_metric_handler_requests_total` and
`promhttp_metric_handler_requests_in_flight`, which the /metrics handler is
wrapped in. None of those are disabled by `--web.disable-exporter-metrics`. Listing any of them would make docs-check fail, since it resolves
documented names from this package's own source.
-->

## ExampleCollector

Defined in `internal/collector/collector.go`. Replace this section's rows when
you adapt `ExampleCollector` into your real collector.

| Metric | Type | Labels | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `@@NAMESPACE@@_example_entries` | Gauge | - | Number of key/value entries parsed from the example data source in the last scrape. |
| `@@NAMESPACE@@_example` | Gauge | `key` | Value reported by the example data source, by key. |

## Self-instrumentation

Each row below is gated by its own `--collector.<name>` flag
(`--collector.command_exec`, `--collector.command_exec_wait`; both default
`true`, negate with `--no-collector.<name>`), the same as any other
collector. See [docs/configuration.md](configuration.md).

| Metric | Type | Labels | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `@@NAMESPACE@@_exporter_command_duration_seconds` | Histogram | `outcome` | Duration in seconds of external commands issued by this exporter's collectors, by outcome (`success` or `error`). Defined in `internal/collector/execute.go`. |
| `@@NAMESPACE@@_exporter_request_wait_seconds` | Histogram | `outcome` | Duration in seconds a command invocation waited for a concurrency slot, by outcome (`success` if a slot was granted, `error` if the caller's own deadline expired first). Both series stay at a permanent zero once `--exporter.max-requests-per-target` is unset (the default). Defined in `internal/collector/limiter.go`. |
| `@@NAMESPACE@@_exporter_collector_success` | Gauge | `collector` | Whether the last scrape of the collector succeeded (1=success, 0=failure). Defined in `internal/collector/status_tracker.go`. |
| `@@NAMESPACE@@_exporter_collector_duration_seconds` | Gauge | `collector` | Duration of the last scrape for the collector, in seconds. Defined in `internal/collector/status_tracker.go`. |
